# Jira Ticket Naming Conventions

This file is the single source of truth for Jira naming conventions.

## Epics

Format: `TEAM::[MVP::]Feature Name`

| Prefix | Team | Scope |
|--------|------|-------|
| `BE::` | Backend | Services, schema, repos, DB |
| `FE::` | Frontend | UI, React components, pages |
| `DE::` | Desktop | Tauri, Rust, native shell |
| `DES::` | Design | Design mockups, UX review |
| `INF::` | Infrastructure | CI/CD, DevOps, tooling |

Add `::MVP::` only if the epic is part of the initial MVP release scope.

Examples: `INF::MVP::Monorepo & Build`, `BE::MVP::Supabase Security`, `FE::Habit Tracking`, `DES::Settings Pages`

## Stories

Format: `Stream::Type::Name`

**Stream** identifies the feature domain (15 options):
Security, Backend, UI, Tasks, Planning, Tray, Stats, Settings, Focus, Habits, Teams, Billing, Admin, DevOps, Testing, Design

**Type** identifies the work kind (10 options):
Schema, Repo, Service, Context, Component, View, Integration, Config, Test, Design

**Exception:** Design stories skip the Type segment and use `Design::Name` directly.

Examples:
- `Security::Schema::RLS Policies`
- `Backend::Service::BreakService`
- `UI::Config::Install Tailwind CSS`
- `Tasks::View::Today View`
- `DevOps::Config::Add Turborepo`
- `Design::Tray Focus Tab — 5-state layout review`

## Rules

- The story Stream prefix and the parent epic's Team prefix are independent — a `Backend::` story can sit under an `FE::` epic.
- The parent field in Jira links a story to its epic; the prefix is for filtering and scanning the board.
- When creating new tickets, always follow these conventions. If unsure which Stream or Type to use, ask.
